                              "text" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/browse/STK-489",
                              "type" : "text"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : " - tried to change Synchonized/Optional to return diff value on operator-> depending on if target w",
                              "type" : "text"
                           },
                           {
                              "type" : "hardBreak"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : "as struct with operator-> - but introduced ambugiity and was bad direction; INSTEAD - DEPRECATED operator-> () in Synchonized - and force explicit use of cget o",
                              "type" : "text"
                           },
                           {
                              "type" : "hardBreak"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : "r rwget() on synchonized to get reference, or load to get a copy.  For synchonized objects - these distrinctions just matter. Still experimental, but buetter do",
                              "type" : "text"
                           },
                           {
                              "type" : "hardBreak"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : "cumetned and I think clearer",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     }
